<article class="env-lemma" id="0E05">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E05">Lemma <span data-tag="0E05">72.11.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $k$. Let $x \in |X|$ be a point with image $y \in |Y|$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
if $f$ is étale at $x$, then $X$ is geometrically reduced at $x$ $\Leftrightarrow $ $Y$ is geometrically reduced at $y$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $f$ is surjective étale, then $X$ is geometrically reduced $\Leftrightarrow $ $Y$ is geometrically reduced. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) is clear because $\mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}} = \mathcal{O}_{Y, \overline{y}}$ if $f$ is étale at $x$. Part (2) follows immediately from part (1). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>